wmcliphist: the Wayland clipboard on XWayland (Big WindowMaker)

On a Wayland session wmcliphist runs on XWayland, and wlroots bridges the
clipboard between X11 and Wayland clients only for an X11 window with the
keyboard focus, which a dock-app never has:

- An item chosen from the menu (or taken up when the application that
  copied quits) also goes to the Wayland clipboard, through
  `big-wm-clipboard --copy` (wl-copy; the content on a pipe). Before, it
  stayed in the X11 CLIPBOARD only, and Ctrl+V in a Wayland client pasted
  the previous copy.
- When the compositor's bridge owns the CLIPBOARD (a copy of a Wayland
  client) and does not answer, wmcliphist no longer takes it up as if the
  application had quit: that replaced the Wayland copy with the last item
  of the history. The copies of Wayland clients reach the menu from the
  history database (big-wm-clipboard --watch records them and sends
  SIGUSR2).
- The history (re)loaded from the database (startup, SIGUSR2) no longer
  takes the selection up: on each reload wmcliphist became the owner,
  found nothing to give and published the first item, which replaced the
  copy of the Wayland client that had just been recorded.

Without WAYLAND_DISPLAY (the X11 session) nothing changes.

diff --git a/wmcliphist/bigwm.c b/wmcliphist/bigwm.c
index 2836137..20a6684 100644
--- a/wmcliphist/bigwm.c
+++ b/wmcliphist/bigwm.c
@@ -75,6 +75,29 @@ bigwm_favorite(const gchar *content, gint locked)
 	run_with_input("--favorite", locked ? "on" : "off", content);
 }
 
+/* A Wayland session: wmcliphist runs on XWayland. */
+gboolean
+bigwm_wayland(void)
+{
+	const gchar *wayland = g_getenv("WAYLAND_DISPLAY");
+
+	return wayland != NULL && *wayland != '\0';
+}
+
+/*
+ * On XWayland, what wmcliphist publishes reaches the Wayland clients only
+ * through the compositor's bridge, and wlroots opens that bridge only to an
+ * X11 window with the keyboard focus, which a dock-app never has: a chosen
+ * item would stay in the X11 CLIPBOARD alone. It also goes to the Wayland
+ * clipboard (wl-copy, through the helper).
+ */
+void
+bigwm_copy(const gchar *content)
+{
+	if (bigwm_wayland())
+		run_with_input("--copy", NULL, content);
+}
+
 /*
  * The saved history, oldest first so that the newest ends on top. Returns 0
  * when the database answered (even empty), -1 without big-wm-clipboard.
